 "text": "Hi, how is your day? Well, it depends on the kind of oil you're using, the type of canvas, and how you're applying the oil. Yeah, six months is a good time frame to start varnishing. It's best to give it a thorough drying time. Well, you can try using a speed up drying agent, but it's best to wait for the oil to dry naturally. Well, you'll be able to see the oil has fully dried when it leaves no oily residue on your fingerprints. You can also try touching the oil with your finger and see if it comes off easily.",
